  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 01f934d50526431a9392a6ceca1dc33d, type: 3}
  m_Name: Rampage Cell Config 1
  m_EditorClassIdentifier:
  CellName: Rampage
  Description: Demolition arena cell, intensity 1 of 4 - a quiet arena you have mostly to yourself: 295
    seeded plants totalling ~49150 prisms of cacti, spires, pines, rosettes and coral,
    filling the volume from just outside the nucleus out to the membrane, across all three
    domains, each plant one of the four elemental variations. Intensity 4 is the shipped,
    play-tested arena EXACTLY; 1 is that same arena made bigger, denser and easier to hit:
    5x the plant count, prisms at 1.6x the authored leaf (bigger is an easier target for the
    cone and an easier surface to skim), a nucleus at prefab scale 500 (~490u radius), 1x
    the authored wildlife, and - authored in the scene, not here - twice as many crystals as
    players. The nucleus stays clear (the planting band is clamped outside it) and is the
    crystals' contested ground. The mature forest is ~7,651,558 volume, and this cell's
    VOLUME thresholds are the play-tested intensity-4 ladder scaled by that - so Frenzy sits
    the same 4.11x above the forest at every level. Collider envelope: up to 50,000 prisms
    (LOD-cullable, and the count backstop freezes growth there) plus 440 always-on
    heart-crystal colliders at the plant cap. Pending an in-editor re-measure; regenerate
    with Tools/Build/rampage_intensity.py rather than hand-editing.
